      "solution": "**Given:**\n\nWe need to find the number which, when added to 20% of 460, equals 70% of 920.\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nLet the number be x .\n\n20% of 460 + x = 70% of 920\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n20% of 460 = 460 × 0.20 = 92\n\n70% of 920 = 920 × 0.70 = 644\n\n92 + x = 644\n\n⇒ = 644 - 92\n\n⇒ x = 552\n\n**The correct answer is option 4.**",
